Yeah, definitely some tradeoffs there. I do like that it makes the common use cases easy. And yeah, I did make quite the &quot;turduckin&quot; as you put it .<p>A more concrete criticism: suppose you wanted to embed some markdown, where all of the content consisted of an indented code block.<p>%markdown: a code block<p><pre><code>    fn foo(){

        # do stuff

    }
</code></pre>
%%<p>My understanding is the leading spaces would be removed, breaking the formatting and making it normal text instead of a code block.
